//! Call-site type-checking: applying a callee scheme to a sequence
//! of type / value arguments.
//!
//! [`synth_call`] is the phase-generic dispatcher: it synthesizes the
//! callee, then routes closed applications through [`apply_mono`].
//! Surface Kio's expression dispatcher routes ordinary calls through
//! [`run_general_ordinary_value`]. A call whose written omissions are
//! connected to nested argument results opens one finite [`GoalStore`] domain
//! and advances its retained expressions through the one-shot [`frontier`]
//! schedule. Kio' never admits those transient goals: it requires universal
//! arguments explicitly and infers only a newtype constructor's tracked
//! existential suffix. Goal-free calls in either phase keep the direct
//! check-against-declared-type path.
//!
//! Two boundary cases live here too: Kio's successive-layer call selector
//! (Prime rejects a single call that spans layers) and
//! [`apply_polymorphic_function`], the direct goal-free polymorphic engine.
//!
//! Extracted from [`super::typecheck_core`] for navigability;
//! depends on the umbrella's [`super::Synth`] / [`super::Typer`]
//! traits plus the rest of the synth / unify machinery.

